18. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS AND TOOLCHAIN ATTRIBUTION
==============================================================================

AdeshLang integrates, interoperates with, or optionally invokes several
third-party compilers, linkers, runtimes, and intermediate representation
frameworks. Each of these components remains the intellectual property of
its respective authors and is governed by its own license terms:

  1. LLVM Project (LLVM, Clang, LLD, LLC, LLVM-AR)
     - License: Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
     - Copyright (c) LLVM Project Contributors
     - Purpose: AdeshLang uses LLVM and Clang for Ahead-of-Time (AOT) machine
       code generation, code optimization (`llc`), object linking (`lld`,
       `lld-link`), and static archiving (`llvm-ar`).
     - Details: https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

  2. MLIR (Multi-Level Intermediate Representation)
     - License: Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
     - Copyright (c) LLVM / MLIR Contributors
     - Purpose: AdeshLang utilizes MLIR dialects (`mlir-opt`, `mlir-translate`)
       for structured high-level intermediate representation lowering, kernel
       transformations, and hardware-accelerated GPU targets (NVVM/ROCDL).
     - Details: https://mlir.llvm.org

  3. Microsoft Visual C++ (MSVC) Runtime & Windows SDK
     - License: Microsoft Software License Terms
     - Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
     - Purpose: On Windows, AdeshLang interfaces with the Microsoft Universal C
       Runtime (UCRT), MSVC CRT (`msvcrt.lib`, `legacy_stdio_definitions.lib`),
       and Windows SDK system libraries (`kernel32`, `user32`, `advapi32`)
       for native PE/COFF execution and linking.
     - Details: https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/license-terms/

  4. GCC & GNU Toolchain (GCC, GNU ld, ar)
     - License: GNU General Public License v3 (GPLv3) with GCC Runtime
       Library Exception
     - Copyright (c) Free Software Foundation, Inc.
     - Purpose: AdeshLang supports GNU GCC and GNU binutils as backend
       linkers and cross-compilation drivers across supported POSIX environments.
     - Details: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/

  5. Cranelift & Wasmtime
     - License: Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions / MIT License
     - Copyright (c) Bytecode Alliance Contributors
     - Purpose: Fast incremental code generation and JIT execution engine.
     - Details: https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime

  6. Cryptographic & Networking Engines
     - Includes components under MIT, Apache 2.0, and BSD licenses (e.g.,
       Rustls, ring, OpenSSL compatibility bindings, AES-GCM, ChaCha20,
       Ed25519, Argon2).

  7. AI Neural Engine & GGUF Runtime
     - Includes components under MIT / Apache 2.0 / PSF License (llama.cpp,
       ggml, Python).

The full text of third-party licenses is available in the THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
directory distributed with AdeshLang.

